{"type": "say", "text": "Good morning, everyone. We're here for the final check on the \"Tidal Memory\" installation plan for Gallery 4, October 12 through 15. The draft plan currently proposes online-connected playback, eight visitor stations, 15-minute sessions, and a 5:00 PM public opening on October 12. Before I can approve this plan, I need to hear from each of you — rights, technical, accessibility, and artist representatives — on whether you have any conditions that must be added. Please go ahead and share any conditions or concerns you have at this time."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF4", "text": "I have an artist-side condition to add. I confirmed with the artist's manager this afternoon that the artist will permit public access on October 12 only from 6:00 PM onward — not 5:00 PM as currently drafted — and will not permit press or invited photographers inside before that opening. The manager's email is awaiting entry in the artist file. These conditions must be reflected in the approved plan."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF2", "text": "Maya, here are my technical conditions. I completed the headset and network test after yesterday's installation rehearsal, and the test report is still in the equipment vendor's queue, so this information hasn't been circulated yet. The approved headset model supports only six simultaneous stations — not eight as currently drafted — and each session must be limited to exactly 12 minutes to prevent thermal shutdown. These are hard technical constraints: the headsets will overheat if we run more than six stations or sessions longer than 12 minutes. So the plan must be revised to reflect six stations and 12-minute sessions before it can be approved."}
```

